-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",128,{
[4065]="70001782\n1\tAsk Mincham to translate the Uruk-orders\tMincham has a small camp overlooking the Greenway just south of the Fields of Fornost. Daervunn returned the orders to you and sent you to speak with Mincham, who is proficient in the Black Speech of Mordor, at his camp bordering the Fields of Fornost in the west. He hopes that Mincham will be able to translate the orders.\n2\tBring Mincham's report to Daervunn\tDaervunn awaits your return at Esteldín. Mincham returned the orders to you and sent you back to Daervunn with his report.\n",
[4066]="700621B4\n1\tBring the scroll to Melynis\tRhiangar has asked you to bring the scroll to Melynis Bragreg. Melynis is among the caravans south of Andrath, in northern Cardolan.\n2\tTalk to Gerwyn\tMelynis has suggested that you speak with Gerwyn while she works on deciphering the scroll. Gerwyn is located in the caravan in northern Cardolan.\n",
[4067]="70028236\n1\tBring the note to Haul at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales\tHaul is at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales. You should bring the note to Haul at once.\n",
[4068]="70017923\n1\tComplete A Worthy Garment\030Complete Hewing a New Stone\tDardúr knows of a legendary rune-keeper who could teach you great lessons, but first you must be suitably outfitted.\n2\tTalk to Dardúr\tDardúr is at Gondamon in Ered Luin.\n3\tTalk to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond's house lies in the vale of Rivendell in the Trollshaws. Dardúr has bidden you seek the guidance of Elrond Halfelven so you might learn from him.\n",
[4069]="70002231\n1\tDefeat Chieftain Nûlthauk\tThe Orc-cave is north of Aughaire, just east of Dûn Covád. Eilig has asked you to slay the Ongburz Chieftain, Nûlthauk who led the Orcs who slew his kindred.\n2\tTalk to Eilig\tEilig is back at Aughaire. Nûlthauk is dead, so you should return to Eilig to tell him the tale of your deeds.\n",
[4070]="70054CA1\n1\tDestroy defiled bones (total: 8)\tDefiled bones can be found in Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow. You should destroy the defiled bones.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed defiled bones within Gorthad Nûr.\n",
[4071]="70054CA9\n1\tDestroy corrupted runes (total: 8)\tCorrupted runes can be found in Gorthad Nûr, the Deep-barrow. You should destroy the corrupted runes.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed corrupted runes within Gorthad Nûr.\n",
[4072]="7006BF7D\n1\tExamine the well for signs of disrepair\tExamine the well for signs of disrepair.\n2\tRemove the stones clogging the drain-ways of the well (total: 3)\tRemove the small stones clogging the drain-ways of the well.\n3\tExamine the well once more\tExamine the well once more.\n4\tAsk Mushêndu in Urmâkh what you should do\tSpeak to Mushêndu in Urmâkh about what to do next.\n5\tFind a large, smooth stone outside Mushêndu's farm\tAcquire a large, smooth stone of the right size from outside Mushêndu's farm. Mushêndu's farm is located just outside Urmâkh to the north-west.\n6\tUse smooth stone on stuck rock inside Urmâkh well\tUse the smooth stone to bash the stuck rock inside Urmâkh well back down.\n7\tSpeak with Mushêndu in Urmâkh\tSpeak with Mushêndu in Urmâkh.\n",
[4073]="700155C9\n1\tHead towards Ânghumu-ru\tÂnghumu-ru is located to the south-west of Anazârmekhem. You should travel towards Ânghumu-ru and search for Feggi there.\n2\tSearch for Feggi at Ânghumu-ru\tFeggi and his dwarves can likely be found in western Ânghumu-ru. You should search for Feggi and his dwarves.\n",
[4074]="70067CB3\n1\tClear graffiti from the walls ([see journal]/6)\tFind the defaced walls throughout Halrax and clean them to restore their beauty.\n2\tSpeak with Hazâl near the dock in Halrax\tHaving cleaned the graffiti from the walls in town, you should return to Hazâl near her home by the docks in Halrax.\n3\tFind the Corsair vandal and ask him to stop\tHazâl asked that you search the south-eastern dock of Halrax for the vandal responsible for defacing the walls throughout the town.\n4\tSpeak with Hazâl near the docks in Halrax\tYou confronted the Corsair vandal, and after issuing a threat and attacking you, he ran when it was clear you would defeat him. Return to Hazâl and inform him that the vandal should no longer be a problem.\n",
[4075]="7001E98C\n1\tDefeat Darúk\030Destroy Darúk's battle-standard\tDarúk is at Ânghum-maudhûl to the east of Mithechad. Harchador has asked you to defeat Darúk and destroy his standard.\n2\tTalk to Harchador at Mithechad\tHarchador is at Mithechad, west of Ânghum-maudhûl. You should return to Harchador with news of your victory against Darúk.\n",
[4076]="7001A298\n1\tDefeat War-leaders in Eregion (total: 10)\tYou have been instructed to defeat War-leaders in Eregion.\n",
[4077]="7001BECC\n1\tGâdhûp and Brúllug can be found in Sarnúr, south of Thorin's Hall, reached through the ruins of Orodost. Snár has asked you to defeat either Gâdhûp the Snow-troll or Brúllug the drake.\t\n2\tTalk to Snár in Thorin's Hall\tSnár is in Thorin's Hall, north of Sarnúr, just outside the Blue Stone Garrison. You should return to Snár and tell him of your victory over the terrors of Sarnúr.\n",
[4078]="70046121\n1\tDefeat heat waves (total: 5)\tHeat Waves can be found in the area near the Party Tree in the Shire. You should defeat Heat Waves.\n2\tSpeak with Tansy Tighfield\tTansy Tighfield is at the Party Tree in the Shire. You should return to Tansy Tighfield.\n",
[4079]="700173BA\n1\tDefeat lieutenants (total: 4)\030Defeat chief guards (total: 4)\tFil Gashan is south-west of Anazârmekhem. Vagun believes that the Orcs of Fil Gashan must be driven out, and that by defeating the lieutenants and taking their gear, you might be able to deceive the other Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Vagun at Anazârmekhem\tVagun is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of Fil Gashan. You fought your way through Fil Gashan and defeated the lieutenants as you were asked. Now you should return to Vagun with your report.\n",
[4080]="70052969\n1\tTalk to Gwaihir the Wind-lord\tGwaihir the Wind-lord can be found at the Eyrie. You should talk to Gwaihir.\n2\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n",
[4081]="7002F920\n1\tDirect archers in the defence of Harwick (total: 4)\030Approach an Easterling\tDirect archers with your flag while defending Harwick. Wulfin has given you a flag you can use to direct the archers defending Harwick.\n2\tTalk to Wulfin\tWulfin is in Harwick.\n",
[4082]="7002F103\n1\tDefeat Easterlings in the defence of Harwick (total: 10)\tThe Easterlings are attacking Harwick. Wulfin has alerted you to the fact that Easterlings are about to descend upon Harwick.\n2\tTalk to Wulfin\tWulfin can be found in Harwick. Wulfin will be pleased to hear Harwick is secure.\n",
[4083]="70009E73\n1\tDefeat minions of Angmar at Hoarhallow (total: 6)\tStay within the bounds of Hoarhallow village and stop the forces of Angmar threatening the hobbits there. Mayor Wat Mudbottom enlisted your aid in fighting back the foes within the area of Hoarhallow.\n2\tTalk to Mayor Wat Mudbottom\tMayor Mudbottom is in Hoarhallow. Now that you have assisted in the defence of Hoarhallow, you should speak with Mayor Wat Mudbottom about the reward he offered you.\n",
[4084]="70009E75\n1\tDefeat minions of Angmar at Lugazag (total: 6)\tFight and slaughter the foes from Angmar within the area of Lugazag. Sergeant-at-Arms Ambeng wants to ensure that the Free Peoples are prepared for the onslaught that will ensue at the walls of Lugazag and enlisted your help in driving the foe from the field. Stay within the immediate area of the tower and stand against the foe. If Ambeng or Lugazag falls, report to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig.\n2\tTalk to Sergeant-at-Arms Ambeng\030Talk to Captain-General Tordúr\tIf Lugazag and Sergeant-at-Arms Ambeng still stand, report to him for your reward. If the tower was lost or Ambeng fell in battle, report to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig. You stood against the foe within the walls of Lugazag. Your efforts were not in vain, and you are owed a well-earned reward.\n",
[4085]="700355DE\n1\tSpeak with Thane Cynegar\tThane Cynegar is in the Mead Hall of Scylfig. You should go to the Thane and tell him that the time for battle draws near.\n2\tTry to comfort Cyneberg\tCyneberg is in the icy ruins of Scylfig. You should comfort Cyneberg after her great loss.\n",
[4086]="7001BF4E\n1\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is eager to discuss the plan over how to protect The Prancing Pony with you in the moments before the assault.\n2\tDefeat the first assault\tThe first assault has begun. The Prancing Pony, and those within, must be protected all costs.\n3\tDefeat the second assault\tThe first assault has been defeated, but the enemy is not broken. The defences must be kept up.\n4\tDefeat the third assault\tThe enemy forces are appearing weak and ragged. Their numbers are dwindling.\n5\tDefeat Goilag\tFor Bree to be a free town once more, Goilag, the leader of the brigands, must be defeated.\n",
[4087]="70029FC4\n1\tComplete 'Defence of The Prancing Pony' in a raid group\tThe women and children of Bree have barricaded themselves within The Prancing Pony Inn. The brigands and ruffians who took the town over are seeking to punish those who stand against them.\n",
[4088]="70009E79\n1\tDefeat minions of Angmar at Tirith Rhaw (total: 6)\tDefeat the foes from Angmar within the area of Tírith Rhaw. Sergeant-at-Arms Mibrethil wants to ensure that the Free Peoples are prepared for the onslaught that will ensue at the walls of Tírith Rhaw and enlisted your help in driving the foe from the field. Stay within the immediate area of the tower and stand against the foe. If Mibrethil or Tírith Rhaw falls, report to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig.\n2\tTalk to Sergeant-at-Arms Mibrethil\030Talk to Captain-General Tordúr\tIf Tírith Rhaw and Sergeant-at-Arms Mibrethil still stand, report to him for your reward. If the tower was lost or Mibrethil fell in battle, report to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig. You stood against the foe within the walls of Tírith Rhaw. Your efforts were not in vain and you are owed a well-earned reward.\n",
[4089]="70009E77\n1\tDefeat minions of Angmar at Tol Ascarnen (total: 6)\tStand with Lieutenant Solvi at Tol Ascarnen and defeat the enemy there. Lieutenant Solvi wants to prepare for battle and hold this all-important location out of the hands of the Enemy. If you succeed, speak with Solvi or if he or Tol Ascarnen falls into enemy hands, report to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig.\n2\tTalk to Lieutenant Solvi\030Talk to Captain-General Tordúr\tReport to Lieutenant Solvi at Tol Ascarnen if he stands and you control the location. If he has fallen or the enemy claimed the keep, return to Glân Vraig and speak with Captain-General Tordúr. The battle at Tol Ascarnen earned you victory over your foes.\n",
[4090]="7002F35E\n1\tDefeat Orcs and trolls in the defence of Walstow (total: 10)\tOrcs and trolls are attacking Walstow. Waldeg asked you to join in the defence of Walstow, protecting it from an army of Orcs and trolls.\n2\tTalk to Waldeg\tWaldeg is at Snowbourn. Waldeg will be pleased to hear that Walstow has been defended.\n",
[4091]="7002FCCC\n1\tTreat injured Rohirrim soldiers during the defence of Walstow (total: 4)\030Use your kit to start treating the soldier\030Approach an injured soldier\tInjured Rohirrim can be found in Walstow. Waldeg asked you to triage and treat the Rohirrim who have been injured defending Walstow.\n2\tTalk to Waldeg\tWaldeg is at Snowbourn. Waldeg will be pleased to hear that you were able to treat the wounds of several injured Rohirrim.\n",
[4092]="70070CFD\n1\tSpeak with Arvunath\tYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.\n2\tDefend Arvunath from the attacking Orcs\tYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.\n3\tDefend Arvunath from the attacking Orcs\tYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.\n4\tDefend Arvunath from the attacking Orcs\tYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.\n5\tDefend Arvunath from the attacking Orcs\tYour mission is to travel to the Elderwell and assist the Sul Madásh scholar Arvunath while she investigates the ruins.\n",
[4093]="70009E78\n1\tDefeat minions of Angmar within the Isendeep Mine (total: 10)\tLieutenant Otur is within the Isendeep Mine. Lieutenant Otur asked for your assistance to help defend the Isendeep Mine against the forces of Angmar. If you succeed, speak with Otur or if he or the Isendeep falls into enemy hands, report to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig.\n2\tTalk to Lieutenant Osur\030Talk to Captain-General Tordúr\tLieutenant Otur is within the Isendeep Mine. If Otur has fallen or the Isendeep Mine is in the hands of the enemy, you can speak with Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig in his stead. Through a hard fought battle, you defeated great number of the enemy within the Isendeep mine.\n",
[4094]="70009E76\n1\tDefeat minions of Angmar at the Grimwood Lumber-camp (total: 6)\tStay within the area of the Grimwood Lumber-camp and defeat the enemy out of Angmar. First Marshal Núrdam believes that the Free Peoples can achieve victory with your assistance at the Grimwood Lumber-camp and has asked that you stay and fight to defeat the foe when they come. If Ambeng or Lugazag falls, report to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig.\n2\tTalk to First Marshal Núrdram\030Talk to Captain-General Tordúr\tFirst Marshal Núrdram is at the Grimwood Lumber-camp. If Núrdram fell in battle or the Lumber-camp has fallen to the enemy, make your way to Glân Vraig and speak with Captain-General Tordúr. Though it was a hard-fought battle, you made your stand and have earned your reward.\n",
[4095]="70065674\n1\tDeliver the materials to Kafaaz at Lugazag\030Collect Grimwood logs ([see journal]/10)\030Collect unrefined Isendeep ore ([see journal]/10)\tHead into the Ettenmoors and collect the materials that are needed to construct a door that will seal the upper levels of Lugazag away from the enemy.\n",
[4096]="7006567A\n1\tDeliver the materials to Dumûl at Lugazag\030Collect Grimwood kindling ([see journal]/1)\030Collect unrefined Isendeep ore ([see journal]/5)\030Collect Grimwood roots ([see journal]/5)\tHead out into the Ettenmoors and collect the materials needed to construct the gate that will seal the front of Lugazag tower.\n",
})
